  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{2}}=$",
  "worked_solution": "A quotient of square roots of two positive numbers is equal to the square root of the quotient of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$",
